From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:08:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Keep the active addon version when a project installs its
 own

Every registered install made its version the machine's active one, and
register_packages() activates the required version of every installed
addon, so configuring one project that declares a version, e.g.
add_addons("name 1.0.0") or a test copy "name v0.0.0-<commit>", switched
the addon for every command outside a project and for every project that
declares no version.

A project locks and pins the versions it declares, so an install made for
it does not need the active version. install_addons marks the xrepo run
with XMAKE_IN_ADDONS_AUTOFETCH (the way the package tools mark their
child runs with XMAKE_IN_XREPO), and activates_addon() in the install
action tells the two places that activate, _register_addon() for a new
install and register_packages() for an installed one, to leave a
top-level requirement that names a version inactive. A new install of it
is pinned in the installing process instead, so the addon's on_test
still sees the version being installed. A declaration without a version
and the addon's dependencies, which the project does not lock, are
activated as before; an addon's first version is always activated, and
`xmake addon --install` / `xrepo install --addon` activate as before.

test_autofetch_keep_active_version installs 2.0.0, lets a project that
declares 1.0.0 install it, and checks that the project loads and locks
1.0.0 while the active version stays 2.0.0; without this change it
fails there (active 1.0.0). The release recipes assert in on_test that
the addon sees the version being installed; without the pin that
assertion fails ("the addon sees 2.0.0 while installing 1.0.0").

Not covered: an on_test that runs xmake in a child process sees the
active version, the pin lives only in the installing process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
